<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tharyps</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. late 5th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> · Also known as Tharypas</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tharyps was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/molossians">Molossians</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epirus">Epirus</a> in the late 5th century BCE. Educated at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>, he is credited by ancient writers with introducing Greek customs, letters and institutions to his kingdom, and he was an ancestor of the later Aeacid kings, including Pyrrhus.</p></div>
